/**
 * @mainpage CPPToolkit public API
 *
 * CPPToolkit is a modular C++ library distributed as one vcpkg package.
 * Enable only the module features required by the application. The CMake
 * targets are named `cpptoolkit::<module>`.
 *
 * @section modules Modules
 *
 * - platform: operating-system and architecture identification.
 * - struct: fixed-capacity data structures, including structs::RingBuffer.
 * - mvvm: observable properties, subscriptions, commands and work queues.
 * - algo: reserved namespace for algorithm integrations.
 * - ui: persistent widgets drawn every frame using Dear ImGui and ImPlot.
 * - net: transport contracts, placeholder serial/TCP backends and optional
 *   SimpleBLE connection management.
 *
 * Enabling ui enables mvvm, which enables struct. The current module helper
 * requests C++23. Tests, examples and this documentation are opt-in.
 *
 * @section ui_binding UI binding and callback contract
 *
 * Widgets poll mvvm::ObservableProperty::Get() during Draw(), and commit user
 * edits through Set() before invoking the widget's event callback. Callbacks
 * execute synchronously on the render thread; programmatic Set() calls do not
 * trigger user-edit callbacks. Observe the property's OnChanged() to listen to
 * changes from any source. Exceptions are not swallowed by widgets.
 *
 * Bound properties and commands must outlive the widgets that reference them.
 * Widget trees, callback assignments and ImGui state belong to the render
 * thread; only property access is mutex-protected. Do not add/remove/destroy
 * widgets from inside an active Draw()/callback traversal. Defer structural
 * changes until after rendering. Use mvvm::Dispatcher for actions that must be
 * marshalled to the render thread.
 *
 * TableWidget::OnSortRequested is a request to the ViewModel, not an automatic
 * in-place sort. It can include the initial default sort and multi-column sort
 * specifications. Popup open/close callbacks describe user transitions;
 * programmatic visibility changes are reflected without these events.
 *
 * Read-only and feedback widgets do not invent setter callbacks. Menu items
 * and buttons execute a bound mvvm::Command before OnClick. Containers own their
 * children; use Widget::Add(), TabBarWidget::AddTab() or SplitterWidget::First()
 * and SplitterWidget::Second() to build their contents.
 *
 * @section gallery TestUI
 *
 * Build `cpptoolkit_ui_demo` with CPPTOOLKIT_BUILD_UI and
 * CPPTOOLKIT_BUILD_EXAMPLES enabled. The TestUI window contains Input,
 * Feedback, Data, Navigation, Layout and Overlay tabs and displays callback
 * events through a ViewModel property. It uses raylib and rlImGui as its
 * graphics backend. Headless unit tests exercise binding and gallery rendering
 * without creating an operating-system window.
 *
 * @section generation Generating documentation
 *
 * Install Doxygen 1.9.5 or newer, configure with CPPTOOLKIT_BUILD_DOCS=ON, and
 * build the cpptoolkit_docs target. HTML is written to `build-directory/docs/html`
 * and XML to `build-directory/docs/xml`. Undocumented public declarations,
 * malformed references and parameter documentation warnings fail generation.
 * All module headers are included even when their compilation is disabled.
 *
 * @section safety Lifetimes and implementation limits
 *
 * Observable subscriptions must be destroyed before their observable owner.
 * Refer to each MVVM type for callback ordering, snapshot and thread behavior.
 * Serial/TCP transport backends and BLE characteristic I/O are placeholders;
 * optional BLE connection management uses SimpleBLE.
 * PasswordWidget masks display only; its bound std::string is not secure storage.
 * ImageWidget does not own or upload textures; the caller must keep the
 * backend texture alive through rendering.
 */

/** @namespace cpptoolkit
 *  @brief Root namespace of the modular toolkit.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::platform
 *  @brief Platform identification utilities.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::structs
 *  @brief Fixed-capacity data structures.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::mvvm
 *  @brief Observable state, commands and thread handoff utilities.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::algo
 *  @brief Namespace reserved for algorithm integrations.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::net
 *  @brief Transport abstraction, placeholder serial/TCP backends and optional BLE connections.
 */
/** @namespace cpptoolkit::ui
 *  @brief Retained widget trees with immediate-mode rendering and MVVM binding.
 */
